course: dictionary
lesson: 15297
title: Skimmed: quick reading and less fat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Skim is a verb, and skimmed is its past form, so it tells you something already happened. «Mia skimmed the story before bed» means she read it quickly, not slowly and carefully.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The flat stone skimmed across the pond» tells you the stone did not sink. It moved lightly over the top of the water. Ask yourself what would fit, then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Skimmed is also a describing word in food. Skimmed milk is milk with the fat (the cream) taken off. In the USA people usually say «skim milk», but in the UK, Ireland and Australia they say «skimmed milk».
fact: Skimmed is the past form of the verb skim.
fact: «Skimmed» can mean read quickly, moved just over the top of something, or taken the top layer off.
fact: Skimmed milk is milk with most of the fat (cream) taken off.
fact: Skimmed milk has less fat than whole milk.
fact: In the UK, Ireland and Australia people say «skimmed milk»; in the USA they usually say «skim milk».
exercise: «Mia skimmed the story before bed.» What does skimmed mean here? | Wrote a long summary | Tore the page out | Read every word very slowly | *Read quickly, looking for the main parts
exercise: «The flat stone skimmed across the pond.» What does skimmed suggest? | *Moved lightly over the top of the water | Sank straight to the bottom | Froze solid | Was painted bright blue
exercise: Which milk has most of the fat (the cream) taken off? | Whole milk | Milk that has been boiled | Chocolate milk | *Skimmed milk
test: «Dad bought skimmed milk, which has less fat than whole milk.» What does skimmed mean in this sentence? | Had been heated until it boiled | Came from a cow in the field | *Had most of the fat taken off | Had been shaken very hard
test: «He skimmed the menu quickly and ordered a sandwich.» Which word is closest in meaning to skimmed here? | Copied out | Ate | Studied carefully | *Glanced over quickly
exam: «The swallow skimmed low over the grass.» What does skimmed mean? | Climbed high into the clouds | *Flew low, just over the top of something | Sat still on a branch | Dived deep under the water
